    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0428" n="1182" xml:id="pg1182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 654.119/62a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-27T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 27, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2865. For Taylor from Hoover:</p>
                <p>Our wheat situation is such that we simply cannot supply Switzerland. We can send
                    some barley and rye for present and after January 1 considerable corn, although
                    exportable surplus is proving very much less than we contemplated. It is
                    absolutely critical that they should draw their grain supplies except corn from
                    India, Australia and the Argentine and that no supplies should be pledged to
                    other neutrals from North America.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
